{"id": "EUVD-2026-96342", "enisaUuid": "09b39de3-7296-3871-af96-841a40f904af", "description": "AstronRPA through 1.1.6 contains a missing tenant authorization check in robot-service that allows authenticated users to read other tenants' shared variables via the get-batch-shared-var endpoint. Attackers can enumerate sequential shared variable IDs and decrypt all-users variables re-encrypted with their own tenant key to recover other tenants' credentials in plaintext.", "datePublished": "2026-10-10T14:35:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:53:09", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/issues/884", "https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa", "https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/blob/v1.1.6/backend/robot-service/src/main/java/com/iflytek/rpa/robot/dao/SharedVarDao.xml#L52-L63", "https://github.com/iflytek/astron-rpa/blob/v1.1.6/backend/robot-service/src/main/java/com/iflytek/rpa/robot/service/impl/SharedVarServiceImpl.java#L197-L255", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/astronrpa-through-1.1.6-cross-tenant-shared-variable-disclosure-via-get-batch-shared-var"], "aliases": ["GHSA-mcqv-c7v8-6mw4", "CVE-2026-108547"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "8b4fb76b-1564-3b21-a289-dda717762908", "product": {"name": "astron-rpa", "vendor": {"name": "iflytek"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.1.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0b74934f-4cf3-35a1-8271-7c620bf739df", "vendor": {"name": "iflytek"}}], "isExploited": false}